From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:05:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] server: Accept a send buffer size of 0 on FreeBSD too.

Windows takes SO_SNDBUF = 0 (no send buffering). FreeBSD's setsockopt()
refuses a value below 1 with EINVAL, as macOS's does, so on FreeBSD (and
a PS5) WSAEINVAL came back. The server already keeps the value without
calling setsockopt() on macOS; do the same on FreeBSD. Steam's common
socket setup sets 0 on each socket and asserted "Unable to set default
socket options, error 10022".
---
 server/sock.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/server/sock.c b/server/sock.c
index 0716b3f..2d8b66b 100644
--- a/server/sock.c
+++ b/server/sock.c
@@ -3399,29 +3399,29 @@ static void sock_ioctl( struct fd *fd, ioctl_code_t code, struct async *async )
         return;
     }
 
     case IOCTL_AFD_WINE_SET_SO_SNDBUF:
     {
         DWORD sndbuf;
 
         if (get_req_data_size() < sizeof(sndbuf))
         {
             set_error( STATUS_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL );
             return;
         }
         sndbuf = *(DWORD *)get_req_data();
 
-#ifdef __APPLE__
+#if defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__FreeBSD__)
         if (!sndbuf)
         {
             /* setsockopt fails if a zero value is passed */
             sock->sndbuf = sndbuf;
             return;
         }
 #endif
 
         if (!setsockopt( unix_fd, SOL_SOCKET, SO_SNDBUF, (char *)&sndbuf, sizeof(sndbuf) ))
             sock->sndbuf = sndbuf;
         else
             set_error( sock_get_ntstatus( errno ) );
         return;
     }
